<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.custody.reads ~ one reading of the vessel key's custody

`lares vault status` reads every standing file the carrier table names and names every private file it does not, then reads the standing vessel's custody door: whether the vessel holds its key (and by which slot), or how many unlock tries stay this boot, or what a pūlama waits on. It opens nothing. Relation carriers print beside a reminder that rotation never repairs a lost relation secret. A pipe reads prose; `json=true` reads the envelope; `--verbose` prints each row whole.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ status · verbose

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`status` params=`~ the custody reading`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`verbose` params=`verbose/true ~ every row whole`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

